Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 01:03:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 087/106] ASoC: qdsp6: q6routing: knobs for the in-call
 injection COPP

The factory stack picks the COPP topology out of ACDB from the front
end's app_type and acdb_id, and was seen opening the in-call injection
session with app_type 69937 (the record one gets 69936). There is no
ACDB here, so expose the three values as module parameters to be swept
against a device running the factory stack.

Swept: app_type and acdb_id are inert on this side (mainline never sends
them to the DSP, they only pick a COPP to reuse), and the topology they
select in the vendor - the default 0x10314 - is accepted by the ADM but
does not get the injected stream into the uplink either.
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6routing.c | 43 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 42 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6routing.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6routing.c
index 75a016469..1e48ddf97 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6routing.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6routing.c
@@ -361,6 +361,27 @@ struct msm_routing_data {
 
 static struct msm_routing_data *routing_data;
 
+/*
+ * What the factory stack feeds the ADM for the in-call injection session.
+ *
+ * It picks the COPP topology out of ACDB from the front-end's app_type and
+ * acdb_id, and was caught opening the injection session with app_type 69937
+ * (the record one gets 69936). We have no ACDB, so these are knobs to sweep
+ * against the reference device; 0 keeps mainline's behaviour.
+ */
+static uint playback_copp_topology;
+module_param(playback_copp_topology, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(playback_copp_topology,
+		 "COPP topology for the in-call injection port (0 = NULL topology)");
+
+static uint playback_app_type;
+module_param(playback_app_type, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(playback_app_type, "app type for the in-call injection port");
+
+static uint playback_acdb_id;
+module_param(playback_acdb_id, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(playback_acdb_id, "ACDB device id for the in-call injection port");
+
 /**
  * q6routing_stream_open() - Register a new stream for route setup
  *
@@ -378,6 +399,7 @@ int q6routing_stream_open(int fedai_id, int perf_mode,
 	struct route_payload payload;
 	struct q6copp *copp;
 	int copp_idx;
+	int app_type, acdb_id;
 	struct session_data *session, *pdata;
 
 	if (!routing_data) {
@@ -405,10 +427,29 @@ int q6routing_stream_open(int fedai_id, int perf_mode,
 
 	payload.num_copps = 0; /* only RX needs to use payload */
 	topology = NULL_COPP_TOPOLOGY;
+	app_type = 0;
+	acdb_id = 0;
+	/*
+	 * The factory stack picks the COPP topology out of ACDB using the
+	 * front-end's app_type/acdb_id, and was seen opening the in-call
+	 * injection session with app_type 69937 (the record one gets 69936).
+	 * There is no ACDB here, so the three values are module parameters to
+	 * be swept by hand against the reference device.
+	 */
+	if (session->port_id == VOICE_PLAYBACK_TX) {
+		if (playback_copp_topology)
+			topology = playback_copp_topology;
+		app_type = playback_app_type;
+		acdb_id = playback_acdb_id;
+		dev_info(routing_data->dev,
+			 "injection copp: topology %#x app_type %u acdb %u\n",
+			 topology, app_type, acdb_id);
+	}
+
 	copp = q6adm_open(routing_data->dev, session->port_id,
 			      session->path_type, session->sample_rate,
 			      session->channels, topology, perf_mode,
-			      session->bits_per_sample, 0, 0);
+			      session->bits_per_sample, app_type, acdb_id);
 
 	if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(copp)) {
 		mutex_unlock(&routing_data->lock);
